issues.evidence:
Section 6.6 (line ~400): "Restricting the analysis to the 15 datasets with an effective sample size of at least 50 left the ordering unchanged." Table 8 column "Tilt gamma=2: upper (ESS >= 50)" shows otherwise:
- DCP (0.765) exceeds the stratified BCCP (0.754) and S-CQR (0.761);
- BCCP and S-CQR swap order;
- SCP (0.532) and DLS (0.530) swap order.

On all datasets every stratified method (0.770-0.833) is above every marginal method (0.550-0.726). In the ESS >= 50 subset the ranges overlap (stratified 0.754-0.825, marginal 0.530-0.765). The sentence before it, "The stratified methods lost less", therefore does not hold in the subset.

The tilt comparisons also carry no test or CI, although ESS is as low as 5.9 (median 49). The ESS used is the minimum over seeds of the whole-test-set ESS (analyze3.py line 317), not the ESS within the upper stratum whose coverage is reported.
